The libraries are compiled Rust code and include the Rust standard library
(std, core and alloc) and the crates it depends on. Except as noted, the
Rust standard library is available under the Apache License, Version 2.0 or
the MIT license, at your option; copyright in it is retained by its
contributors. Two parts of it are not dual-licensed this way and carry
copyright notices of their own: compiler-builtins (MIT and Apache-2.0 WITH
LLVM-exception, partly derived from LLVM's compiler-rt) and libm (MIT,
partly derived from musl). The end of this file names the Rust toolchain
that built the libraries and reproduces the license files of both from that
toolchain's sources. RUST_STANDARD_LIBRARY_COPYRIGHT.html, next to this
file, is that toolchain's own notice file for the Rust standard library
(COPYRIGHT-library.html) and covers the other crates the standard library
depends on.


